window.DW_MOUNTS = {"source":"https://dragonwilds.runescape.wiki/w/Mount","generatedAt":"2026-10-09T16:39:40.311Z","mounts":{"Terrorbird":{"name":"Terrorbird","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt"],"obtain":"This variant is automatically unlocked when completing The Wild Hunt.","lore":"The nature spirits of Ashenfall serve a purpose, one denied to them by the encroaching Wither. It may seem counterintuitive to have to slay these spirits in order to bind them, but that's what nature is. It's hunt and be hunted. Kill and be killed, life is a perpetual cycle - Everything chained together.","vestige":null},"Infernal Blightbeak":{"name":"Infernal Blightbeak","base":"terrorbird","quests":["Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"Bought from Domri - The Merchant.","lore":"This Breed of terrorbird was the bane of most normal human residents. They would raid farms, culling livestock and devouring grain. They would storm through settlements, smashing to pieces anything within their reach. Only the Black Knights of Dowdun Reach had any success in training them, and only such madmen would even try to.","vestige":"MOUNT: Infernal Blightbeak"},"Crimson Crybaby":{"name":"Crimson Crybaby","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"Dropped from red dragon, KotHaar-Kal, kalphite guardian or found in chests in Umbral Sands.","lore":"A breed created by a Zamorakian priest who found them far less terrifying than he had hoped. Instead of bringing fear to the masses, these terrorbirds would whimper and sob whenever forced to do any manual labour. He named the breed \"crybaby\" in frustration, though it remains disappointingly apt.","vestige":"MOUNT: Crimson Crybaby"},"Mossbeak Hunter":{"name":"Mossbeak Hunter","base":"terrorbird","quests":["Withering Heights"],"obtain":"Bought from Death.","lore":"While many terrorbirds were bred for speed, the mossbeak hunter was bred to pursue. Wild Knights would raise them to chase down dangerous prey, tiring their quarry our from their terrorbird's almost limitless stamina.","vestige":"MOUNT: Mossbeak Hunter"},"Springdown Runner":{"name":"Springdown Runner","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt"],"obtain":"Dropped from green dragons, zogres, soulstone sentinels and chests found in Fellhollow.","lore":"The springdown runner was bred for the races. It was quick, focused and not easily distracted by various tricks of the watching crowd. While nowadays there's less of that racing instinct, this breed of terrorbird still enjoys a good run around.","vestige":"MOUNT: Springdown Runner"},"Grassfoot Screecher":{"name":"Grassfoot Screecher","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt"],"obtain":"Dropped from green dragons, zogres, soulstone sentinels and chests found in Fellhollow.","lore":"Druids in Brynmoor would rear these birds not as mounts, but as guard dogs for their sacred sites. The terrorbirds were raised to be quick, silent and merciless in their defence of the groves.","vestige":"MOUNT: Grassfoot Screecher"},"Leafwood Strider":{"name":"Leafwood Strider","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt"],"obtain":"Dropped from green dragons, zogres, soulstone sentinels and chests found in Fellhollow.","lore":"Druids in Brynmoor would rear these birds not as mounts, but as guard dogs for their sacred sites. The terrorbirds were raised to be quick, silent and merciless in their defence of the groves.","vestige":"MOUNT: Leafwood Strider"},"Oakfeather Raptor":{"name":"Oakfeather Raptor","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Withering Heights"],"obtain":"Bought from Death.","lore":"A green-feathered variant of the terrorbird, popular with the Wild Knights back in the earliest days of Bramblemead. They would raise the raptor from the moment they hatched, so that the bird could imprint on the knight and create a bond of loyalty unlike any other.","vestige":"MOUNT: Oakfeather Raptor"},"Coastal Sunbeak":{"name":"Coastal Sunbeak","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Black Knight's Fortress"],"obtain":"Bought from Evil Emporium.","lore":"Raised along the beaches and coastal regions, the Sunbeak is a colourful terrorbird variant who enjoyed a more fish heavy diet then most.","vestige":"MOUNT: Coastal Sunbeak"},"Summerbellied Wagtail":{"name":"Summerbellied Wagtail","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Black Knight's Fortress"],"obtain":"Dropped from blue dragons, lesser demons, elite Black Knights and chests found in Dowdun Reach.","lore":"This friendly breed of terrorbird is so named because they wag their tails in the presence of their handlers. They delight in playful displays of affection, such as jumping up and down, or attempting to chew someone's face off. Oh, how sweet.","vestige":"MOUNT: Summerbellied Wagtail"},"Eclipseborn Sharpbeak":{"name":"Eclipseborn Sharpbeak","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Black Knight's Fortress"],"obtain":"Dropped from blue dragons, lesser demons, elite Black Knights and chests found in Dowdun Reach.","lore":"Legends says that this breed of terrorbird appears only during a solar eclipse. They are said to possess magical powers; the exact nature of which varies with each telling. In truth, they can hatch just like any terrorbird does and possess no known metaphysical capabilities.","vestige":"MOUNT: Eclipseborn Sharpbeak"},"Sunkissed Clawfoot":{"name":"Sunkissed Clawfoot","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Black Knight's Fortress"],"obtain":"Dropped from blue dragons, lesser demons, elite Black Knights and chests found in Dowdun Reach.","lore":"These bright yellow creatures love nothing more than ferreting out strange green herbs with their sharp claws. They enjoy running around plains, making screeching noises.","vestige":"MOUNT: Sunkissed Clawfoot"},"Astralbeak Warbler":{"name":"Astralbeak Warbler","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Black Knight's Fortress"],"obtain":"Bought from Evil Emporium.","lore":"Named after the stars, rather than the runes, the astralbeak warbler is a strange beast. On nights where the sky is clear and the moon absent, this breed of terrorbird loves nothing more than to raise its head to the heavens and warble strangely haunting melodies.","vestige":"MOUNT: Astralbeak Warbler"},"Zamorakian Pledgesaddle":{"name":"Zamorakian Pledgesaddle","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"Bought from Domri - The Merchant.","lore":"Popular with the Black Knights of Dowdun Reach due to the dark and sinister colour schemes. Many of the knights would ride into battles atop these creatures, screaming about the power of chaos as they went.","vestige":"MOUNT: Zamorakian Pledgesaddle"},"Scorchsummer Ashbeak":{"name":"Scorchsummer Ashbeak","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"Dropped from red dragon, KotHaar-Kal, kalphite guardian or found in chests in Umbral Sands.","lore":"This breed is so named because the breeder's daughter thought they were sunburned when she first saw the chicks. Bright pink and screeching, she immediately put them in buckets of water, only to face the wrath of their mother.","vestige":"MOUNT: Scorchsummer Ashbeak"},"Applefeather Mosstail":{"name":"Applefeather Mosstail","base":"terrorbird","quests":["The Wild Hunt","Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"Dropped from red dragon, KotHaar-Kal, kalphite guardian or found in chests in Umbral Sands.","lore":"This brightly coloured breed of terrorbird gets its name from the apple orchard where the breed was first reared. The owner of the orchard had little imagination for colour combination, so when he saw red and green together the only thing that came to mind were the apples right in front of him. This is in no way similar to the naming process used by the narrative designers.","vestige":"MOUNT: Applefeather Mosstail"},"MOUNT: Magic Carpet":{"name":"MOUNT: Magic Carpet","base":"magic carpet","quests":["Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"This variant is automatically unlocked when completing a section of Icthlarin's Little Helper.","lore":"A carpet, woven from enchanted thread. Summon it to carry you across the desert. Unlike terrorbirds, the carpet will glide smoothly across the desert, showing you a whole new world of sandy sight.","vestige":null},"Uzzerian Umber":{"name":"Uzzerian Umber","base":"magic carpet","quests":["Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"This variant is unlocked when studying the MOUNT: Uzzerian Umber vestige dropped from Tok-Xil in Umbral Sands.","lore":"The light umber tone is handcrafted by Uzzer children as part of their daily lessons. The youngsters gather round and work together to weave the complicated pattern throughout the tapestry as a means of teaching them patience as well as some useful life skills. If you look very carefully, you can see where the garou cubs have found clever ways to sneakily weave in swear words, personal symbols and odd little doodles to amuse themselves. This way, each of the carpets is unique, if not entirely desirable.","vestige":"MOUNT: Uzzerian Umber"},"Manafem Midnight":{"name":"Manafem Midnight","base":"magic carpet","quests":["Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"There are currently no known drop sources or acquisition methods available for this item.","lore":"","vestige":"MOUNT: Manafem Midnight"},"Scorchweave Rug":{"name":"Scorchweave Rug","base":"magic carpet","quests":["Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"There are currently no known drop sources or acquisition methods available for this item.","lore":"","vestige":"MOUNT: Scorchweave Rug"},"Moonsilk Weave":{"name":"Moonsilk Weave","base":"magic carpet","quests":["Icthlarin's Little Helper"],"obtain":"This variant is unlocked when studying the MOUNT: Moonsilk Weave vestige dropped from Kalphite Queen in Umbral Sands.","lore":"Legends tells us that this carpet is woven from the silk of the moon spirits of the Umbral Sands. It is said that they create those silken threads only on clear nights when the moon is full and the stars look down and give them permission. These rare carpets, therefore, only appear in times of great peace and tranquility. Traits that the Umbral Sands have not seen in some time.","vestige":"MOUNT: Moonsilk Weave"}}};
